    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by the elite 87.42 efficiency score of **Yordan Alvarez**. Slotted into the #2 spot against the mid-rotation arm of Melton, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite xwOBA profile and favorable park factors. We are equally aggressive on **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns a 76.65 score despite a tough matchup against Freddy Peralta; the decision to start him is driven entirely by our league's scarcity of stolen bases, as Peralta\u2019s slow delivery offers an optimal environment for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to capitalize on his speed. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (72.82) finds a strong platoon advantage against S. Lugo, and **Trea Turner** (65.28) remains a high-floor foundational piece at the top of our order.\n\nOur most critical bench decision involved **Pedro Ramirez**, who fell just short of the starting threshold with a 41.71 score. While his versatility is appreciated, his projected #8 spot in the order significantly suppressed his value, leading the optimizer to prefer the higher lineup placement and platoon utility of **Luke Raley** (51.95) and **Casey Schmitt** (47.65). Risks remain, specifically surrounding **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose scores are predicated on pending lineup confirmations. We have also flagged **Caleb Durbin** for concern; despite an elite 60% SB projection, his efficiency dropped to 46.70 due to the high-skill profile of Cam Schlittler, making him a marginal play today. We will monitor the weather in all venues, but for now, the Zebras are set to maximize category depth.",
